  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Cumene is an organic compound obtained by&nbsp;Friedel-Crafts alkylation of benzene with&nbsp;propylene. Upon oxidation of cumene (isopropylbenzene) in the presence of air, cumene hydroperoxide is obtained. Upon further treatment of cumene hydroperoxide with dilute acid, phenols are obtained</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fcf5eb83-62a7-459e-a470-19df030d523f-image.png\" style=\"width: 576px; height: 223px;\" /><br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cfa231b9-ed95-4696-81cd-54f46a97cb65-image.png\" style=\"width: 378px; height: 262px;\" /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/10b2e2cd-d7e1-4988-9e43-8b4cbb654e2c-image.png\" style=\"width: 643px; height: 229px;\" /></p>",
